# Cloudflare Pages response headers (docs/DEPLOY_CLOUDFLARE.md). Rules are cumulative: a path that matches several blocks
# gets all of their headers, and a header set by two blocks is sent with both values joined. So a header that differs for
# /admin/ (the Content-Security-Policy) is set only in the /admin/* block, and nothing here is set twice.
#
# No script-src (or any other) Content-Security-Policy on the public pages: Astro inlines its small scripts, so a policy that
# works would have to allow 'unsafe-inline' scripts, which makes it decoration. The site makes no third-party requests anyway
# (CLAUDE.md). The one policy there is, a frame-src, is on /projects/* below.
# No Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy anywhere: the GitHub sign-in popup talks back to /admin/ through window.opener, and
# `same-origin` would cut that link and break the login.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()

# Playable projects embed a game from its own address (the playUrl field, docs/CONTENT_MODEL.md). frame-src is the only
# directive: this page may frame that one origin and no other, and nothing else about scripts or images is restricted. It is on
# /projects/* and not on /*, because the YouTube player on vlog and blog pages is a frame too and would be blocked, and because
# /admin/* sets its own policy (rules are cumulative: a second CSP there would be enforced as well as the admin's and break its
# preview frame). Adding a game means adding its host here (explicit, no wildcard), and if a game moves, change it to match its playUrl: tests/headers.spec.js fails when an embedded
# playUrl in src/content/projects/ is not covered by this line.
/projects/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-src https://vesper.r7orbit.io

# Built assets have a content hash in the file name, so they never change under the same URL.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Self-hosted fonts keep their names, so a month, not forever.
/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000

# The admin is never indexed (it is also noindex in its HTML, disallowed in robots.txt and left out of the sitemap).
#
# Its Content-Security-Policy is what protects the GitHub token the editor keeps in the browser:
#   script-src 'self'    only the bundled editor runs (Decap is bundled by Astro, nothing comes from a CDN). It also needs
#                        'unsafe-eval': Decap checks its config with Ajv, which builds validators with new Function(). No
#                        inline scripts are allowed, and connect-src below stops anything from sending the token elsewhere
#   style-src 'unsafe-inline'  Decap writes its styles at run time (emotion), and so does the live preview
#   img-src              blob: for an image that is chosen or uploaded and not yet saved (Decap holds it as a blob: URL),
#                        avatars.githubusercontent.com for the signed-in author's avatar, raw.githubusercontent.com in case
#                        the editor shows a repository file by its raw address
#   connect-src          api.github.com, the editor's backend; blob: because Decap reads an uploaded image back with fetch()
#                        to keep a local draft backup and to build the commit (without it Save fails with "Failed to
#                        fetch"); www.githubstatus.com, which Decap polls every 5 minutes to warn when GitHub is down.
#                        Neither blob: nor the status page can carry the token anywhere: a blob: URL is local to this tab
#   media-src, worker-src  not set on purpose: the editor has no audio, video or file widgets and starts no workers, so
#                        they fall back to default-src 'self'
#   frame-ancestors      nobody may embed the editor
# The sign-in popup (workers/cms-auth/) is a window of its own, so it needs no entry here. If the editor ever needs
# another address (a different backend, an image host), add it here or the browser blocks it and the console says so.
# tests/headers.spec.js loads /admin/ with this policy applied and fails on any violation.
/admin/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
  Cache-Control: no-store
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-eval'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://avatars.githubusercontent.com https://raw.githubusercontent.com; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' blob: https://api.github.com https://www.githubstatus.com; frame-src 'self' blob:; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
